messages:
ajit: Quick sync — finalizing SDK retry defaults for streaming vs non-streaming. Two quick things we need agreement on: 1) default exponential backoff params for 429 vs 5xx (base, max, retries, jitter). 2) streaming resume behavior: auto-resume vs expose token only. Also auth/idempotency needs: should SDKs automatically attach Idempotency-Key when user doesn't provide one? PR reference: sdk-js #342. Thoughts?

maria: For 429s treat them as rate limits (longer backoff). My suggestion: 429 -> base 800ms, max 8s, up to 4 retries with full jitter. 5xx -> base 300ms, max 4s, up to 2 retries. Always respect Retry-After if present.

kelly: Agree on respecting Retry-After. Regarding auto Idempotency-Key: bad idea to silently inject for users — it can hide duplicate semantics. We should surface a helper to generate and document it, but default to not auto-attach unless user enables "autoIdempotency: true".

sam: FYI dedicated customers often ask to disable client-side retries (they rely on server-side retries/metrics). So SDK default should be conservative and configurable: retryMode = "standard" | "aggressive" | "none".

ajit: Proposal to converge: non-streaming defaults -> full jitter exp backoff; 429: base 700ms max 8000ms retries 4; 5xx: base 300ms max 4000ms retries 2. streaming defaults -> no automatic resume, but SDK must expose resume_token on disconnect and provide a helper resumeOnce(token) that users can opt-in to call. Idempotency -> require user-provided Idempotency-Key for repeated semantic operations, but add helper genIdempotencyKey(). I'll draft RFC and update PR. Anyone opposed?

maria: One nuance for streaming: some languages (Python asyncio) can more reliably resume than browser fetch streams. I'd prefer default resume helper implementations per-platform: for Node/Python provide resume helper, for browser default to opt-in only.

kelly: Sketch for JS handling of Retry-After parsing + jitter (putting this here for the SDK PR):
```
// simple retry delay calc
function calcDelay(base, attempt, max) {
  const exp = Math.min(max, base * Math.pow(2, attempt));
  // full jitter
  return Math.random() * exp;
}
async function shouldRetry(res, attempt) {
  if (res.status === 429) {
    const ra = res.headers.get('Retry-After');
    if (ra) return parseInt(ra, 10) * 1000; // honor header in ms
    return calcDelay(700, attempt, 8000);
  }
  if (res.status >= 500 && res.status < 600) {
    return calcDelay(300, attempt, 4000);
  }
  return null;
}
```

sam: Good snippet. For Go SDK, add context cancellation hook so users can cancel retries mid-flight. And for streaming include sequence numbers in events to help server-side resume verification (not just token).

ajit: Noted. About resume token header — we'll standardize on `x-resume-token` and `x-seq` for sequence number on events. SDKs should expose both when available.

ci-bot: buildbot: CI: sdk-js PR #342 — tests passed on Node 18, 20.

kelly: Quick review ping: @ajit, @maria — can you take a look at the updated tests in #342? I added a python-ish behavior test in the suite too.

ajit: On it, aiming to review today. After we merge, I'll open issues tracking per-language opt-in defaults (browser vs node vs python vs go).

maria: One last detail — docs must show example of client code with Idempotency-Key and how to combine with retries. I'll add a short snippet to the RFC.

ajit: Perfect. I'll post the RFC link in this thread once drafted. Thanks all :thumbsup:
